# rsync --exclude patterns for bin/sync-dotfiles and bin/sync-dotfiles-prune.
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# Pattern syntax matches rsync's --exclude (glob-style, not full gitignore).
#
# Whenever you add a new tracked app (e.g., a new editor or terminal),
# add its cache/state subdirs here so they don't end up in the repo.
#
# Tuned against Chrome 126+, Ferdium 6.x, Firefox 130+, VSCode 1.9x,
# Cursor 0.4x. Re-verify if you upgrade any of those.

# === Editor / OS metadata ===
*.swp
*.swo
*.bak
*~
.DS_Store
.Trash-*

# === Locks / IPC (created by Chrome, Firefox, Electron apps, etc.) ===
*.lock
*.lck
LOCK
LOCKFILE
SingletonLock
.parentlock
Socket
.sock
.lockfile

# === Per-machine / per-user overrides ===
*.local
machine-id

